  "body": "### What is the issue with the Compatibility Standard?\n\nThis is a [\"property mapping\"](https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#css-property-mappings), but it doesn't appear to be specified anywhere what that means. `-webkit-box-orient` and `flex-direction` do not have any keywords in common, so it's unclear how you would convert one to the other.\n\n(As a side note, do we really need these as a mandatory thing? The only sites I've come across that use these `-webkit-` properties also have the modern ones specified.)",
